# SFT execution status v0.92

2026-09-14. The newly approved one-shot Source failure-summary diagnostic read
99,267 bytes using two HTTPS GETs, below the 4 MiB cap. It stopped with
`summary_unavailable_or_incomplete`. No raw log, parameter value or exception
message was retained. No failed-test names were recovered; this does not mean
there were no failures. The attempt marker and STOP evidence are preserved.

## Local parser correction

A synthetic example reproduced a real limitation in the initial parser: its
completion check required an equals-sign-decorated footer and rejected a plain
`1 failed in 1.00s` footer. The repository sets pytest `addopts = "-q"`.
This establishes a local coverage gap, not the actual format or cause of the
remote diagnostic failure: the raw log was not retained and was not fetched again.

A new pure parser, `scripts/parse_sft_source_failure_summary_v2.py`, accepts both
plain and decorated whole-line footers. It checks FAILED and ERROR counts
separately before deduplication, rejects duplicate counts and incomplete rows,
strips all parameter values, and only returns bound test identifiers and
unambiguous allowlisted error types (or null). It contains no download or retry
path. The original diagnostic script was not changed after its one-shot read.

The corrected parser passes 22 synthetic tests on Python 3.11.15 and 3.13.7.
Targeted Ruff checks pass. No real log has been tested with the new parser.

## What remains unresolved

The Source suite's failing test names and exact exceptions remain unknown.
The separate native `source_admission / fixture_failed` cause is also unknown.
Previously verified GitHub lint, isolated controls, validators and Spark results
remain pass; full Source and native qualification remain fail. Gate 5 is not done.

No new commit, push, CI retry, native retry, GPU, real-checkpoint import or training
occurred. The current commit remains `6585a1e073a6a5302630ed63a3c1a3d81adda429`.
The new parser and these records are local and unpublished.

One fresh bounded log read using a corrected successor would require new user
approval. Do not reuse or delete the consumed marker or silently refetch the log.

Records:

- `evidence/lumi-4b-sft-source-failure-summary-diagnostic-v0.1.json`
- `evidence/lumi-4b-sft-source-failure-summary-parser-correction-v0.1.json`
